# VkImageUsageFlagBits census over the three TU_IMG_INV=1 game inventories, generated 2026-11-21.
#
# Question: the inventories published so far counted tiling, UBWC and MUTABLE lists, never the
#   `usage=` mask - so an application path that is announced by a usage bit and nothing else would
#   be invisible. Fragment shading rate (VRS) and fragment density map are exactly such paths, and
#   the FDM one gates a driconf option (journal 34.2, `tu_disable_conservative_fdm_binning`).
#
# Inputs (results/raw/ is gitignored: full proton stdout/stderr; curated copies live in results/):
#   results/raw/game-patched-imginv4.log          859702 B  sha256 cde39e2971a60097...
#   results/raw/game-patched-imginv5.log          976648 B  sha256 80d433927103ef02...
#   results/raw/game-patched-stockflaginv.log    2229411 B  sha256 b297168ac43b30ca...
# Builds (as in results/imginv-3variants.txt): imginv4 = ship stack without 0014 (0001..0013);
#   imginv5 = the ship stack with 0014 (050375a18b7b); stockflaginv = stock Mesa 27 6dfa32a +
#   exp-14 + one line ubwc_all_formats_compatible (32d20074b8a128e4). So the three logs are also
#   a control on the UBWC patches: they must not change the usage surface, and they do not.
#
# Bit values checked against include/vulkan/vulkan_core.h in the mesa checkout (6dfa32a:2814-2820):
#   FRAGMENT_SHADING_RATE_ATTACHMENT_BIT_KHR = 0x100, FRAGMENT_DENSITY_MAP_BIT_EXT = 0x200.
#
# Regenerate:
#   python3 scripts/imginv-usage-bits.py results/raw/game-patched-imginv4.log \
#       results/raw/game-patched-imginv5.log results/raw/game-patched-stockflaginv.log
# Counts differ by one to nine lines from results/imginv-3variants.txt because lines cut by
# foreign stderr are skipped here as well (the per-file note says how many).

